# Scalability and Performance Rules

## Scalability Principles

### 1. Design for Scale
- Always consider scalability from the start
- Design systems that can handle growth
- Implement horizontal scaling capabilities
- Plan for capacity increases

### 2. Configuration-Driven Scaling
- Use configuration to control scaling behavior
- Provide easy switching between configurations
- Implement environment-specific optimizations
- Document scaling strategies

### 3. Resource Management
- Monitor resource usage continuously
- Implement appropriate resource limits
- Plan for resource scaling
- Optimize resource utilization

## Load Configuration

### 1. Dual Configuration System
- Implement standard and high-load configurations
- Provide easy switching between configurations
- Document configuration differences
- Test both configurations thoroughly

### 2. Configuration Parameters
- Database connection pools (20 vs 100 connections)
- API instances (1 vs 3 instances)
- Memory allocation (256MB vs 512MB Redis)
- Monitoring and observability

### 3. Configuration Switching
- Provide simple commands for switching
- Validate configuration changes
- Ensure smooth transitions
- Document switching procedures

